<section class="hero">
  <div class="shell hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow"><i></i> Independent security research studio</span>
      <h1>We find the <em>crack</em> before it becomes the breach.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">RETAK investigates browser, mobile, and web trust boundaries. Every published claim is backed by reproducible evidence and an honest account of impact.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">View the CVE record <span>↗</span></a>
        <a class="button ghost" href="<%= base('/method/') %>">How we verify</a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-footnote"><span>Based in Indonesia</span><span>Coordinated disclosure only</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="fracture-stage" aria-label="An abstract glass fracture representing a security boundary under examination">
      <span class="stage-word" aria-hidden="true">trust<br>boundary</span>
      <span class="glass-plane glass-plane-one" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="glass-plane glass-plane-two" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="glass-shard glass-shard-one" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="glass-shard glass-shard-two" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="glass-shard glass-shard-three" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="fracture-orb" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="orb-light"></span>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 640 640" role="presentation">
          <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round">
            <path d="M321 318 181 92M321 318 468 71M321 318 579 251M321 318 542 491M321 318 356 612M321 318 113 548M321 318 46 292"/>
            <path d="m181 92 84 117-72 47 128 62M468 71l-67 139 53 48-133 60M579 251l-136 31-22 74-100-38M542 491l-121-135-80 72-20-110M356 612l-15-184-89-32 69-78M113 548l139-152-47-86 116 8M46 292l159 18 48-70 68 78"/>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <span class="orb-core">R</span>
      </div>
      <span class="fracture-label fracture-label-source">source</span>
      <span class="fracture-label fracture-label-guard">missing guard</span>
      <span class="fracture-label fracture-label-impact">impact</span>
      <div class="stage-record"><small>Public record</small><strong>05 CVEs</strong><span>Edge · Firefox · Safari</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="metric-strip">
  <div class="shell metric-grid">
    <div class="metric-definition"><strong>re·tak</strong><span>Indonesian · a crack or fracture</span></div>
    <div><strong>05</strong><span>Public CVEs</span></div>
    <div><strong>03</strong><span>Vendors</span></div>
    <div><strong>03</strong><span>Browser families</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section research-section cve-section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Coordinated disclosure</span><h2>Public<br><em>CVE record.</em></h2></div>
      <p>Five fixed vulnerabilities across major browser families. Every entry links directly to its canonical CVE and vendor advisory.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cve-ledger">
<% @discoveries.each_with_index do |discovery, index| %>
<%= discovery_row(discovery, index: index + 1) %>
<% end %>
    </div>
    <a class="section-link" href="<%= base('/discoveries/') %>">Open the canonical CVE archive <span>↗</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section method-preview">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Research method</span><h2>Follow the <em>fracture.</em></h2></div>
      <p>The workflow separates an interesting code path from a vulnerability worth reporting.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="method-grid">
      <article><span>01</span><h3>Model the boundary</h3><p>Map actors, data, authority, expected guards, and the security promise under test.</p></article>
      <article><span>02</span><h3>Trace source to sink</h3><p>Use focused LLM-assisted review to connect attacker control to a sensitive operation.</p></article>
      <article><span>03</span><h3>Build the oracle</h3><p>Test the earliest unknown edge with exact artifacts, positive controls, and guarded negatives.</p></article>
      <article><span>04</span><h3>Prove the impact</h3><p>Promote only reproducible, attacker-observable consequences with honest limitations.</p></article>
    </div>
    <a class="section-link" href="<%= base('/method/') %>">Read the complete method <span>↗</span></a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="contact-band">
  <div class="shell contact-grid">
    <div><span class="eyebrow">Work with RETAK</span><h2>Found a trust boundary worth a <em>closer look?</em></h2></div>
    <div><p>Available for authorized security research, source review, and research collaboration.</p><a class="button primary" href="mailto:jodyritonga@gmail.com">jodyritonga@gmail.com</a></div>
  </div>
</section>
